{
	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - User - MFA - Okta MFA Factors Reset for a User",
	"Description": "Every MFA factor on an account was reset. After a reset the account can enrol a new factor on the next sign-in, so an adversary with a stolen password resets the factors and then enrols their own device.\n\nEvent type: user.mfa.factor.reset_all\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/elastic/detection-rules/integrations/okta/credential_access_attempt_to_reset_mfa_factors_for_okta_user_account/\n- https://github.com/elastic/detection-rules/tree/main/rules/integrations/okta/credential_access_attempt_to_reset_mfa_factors_for_okta_user_account.toml\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"Duration": -900,
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
	"ScheduledType": "search",
	"GUID": "18473156-7ae0-5db5-bbdf-8432d77b2f7b",
	"SearchReference": "74c635b1-f8ba-56a6-91b4-1c5281ce1753"
}